# ---- Secrets: NEVER commit these ----
.env
.env.*
!.env.perps.example
# Template files that carry NO secrets and MUST ship: the README of each
# package tells the reader to copy one. They were silently excluded by the
# `.env.*` rule above -- found when `lighter_adaptive_ensemble_bots/.env.example`
# turned out to exist on disk and never in a commit.
!*.env.example
!**/.env.example
*.key
*.pem
secrets.json
CREDENTIALS_REFERENCE.md

# ---- Python ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ---- Logs & runtime data ----
*.log
*.csv
data/
*.sqlite
*.db

# ---- Sniper / digest runtime state (machine-local; Railway seeds its own) ----
sniper_data/
# `reports/*` and NOT `reports/` — git never descends into an excluded
# DIRECTORY, so with the bare form the negation below is dead. Verified: with
# `reports/`, `git check-ignore -v reports/expansion_research_log.md` still
# reports it ignored by that very line.
reports/*
# [2026-09-11] reports/ was ignored as "digest runtime state" and the fleet's
# JUDGEMENT LAYER then moved in behind that line: the research log's ~20
# refutations, every daily brief, every weekly verdict, and every evidence
# review with its hand-written human layer -- all in ONE un-backed-up copy
# that no worktree and no fresh clone could see. A negation cannot re-include
# a file whose parent directory is excluded, which is why the line above is
# `reports/*`, not `reports/`.
#
# ALL MARKDOWN IS TRACKED -- Eamon, 11-Sep: "track the rest too", after the
# narrow version (the research log alone) shipped and the 115-file / 1.3 MB
# scope was put to him. Scanned before committing, twice and independently: a
# pattern grep for connection strings, keys, tokens and passwords found
# nothing, and `gitleaks --config .gitleaks.toml` over 1.43 MB reported no
# leaks. THE REPO IS PUBLIC -- these carry real-money equity and per-book
# performance, the same class CLAUDE.md already publishes. A decision, not an
# accident.
#
# `.superseded-*.md` are tracked too, deliberately: those files exist BECAUSE
# `preserve_existing_report` refuses to destroy a human layer on a re-run, so
# excluding them would re-create the loss that mechanism prevents.
# Machine state under reports/ stays ignored -- `reports/*` never negates
# .json/.py/.log, so brain_state.json and the census logs do not follow.
!reports/*.md

# ---- Backups / editor / OS cruft ----
*.bak
*.~*
.DS_Store
.fuse_hidden*
untitled folder/

# ---- macOS launchd service file (not used on Railway) ----
com.eamon.tri-arb.plist

# SQLite sidecar files
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-*
scripts/.tape_cache/
scripts/.funding_cache.json
scripts/.dirfund_cache.json
scripts/.tiderider_perp_cache.json

# ---- Backtest caches (scripts/ hidden json = offline-rerun caches, ~10MB) ----
# NOTE: .claude/settings.local.json stays TRACKED on purpose (15-Jul #55/#56:
# it mirrors the claude-code-remote allowlist to every checkout).
scripts/.*.json
# [2026-08-20 (sc)] and the PICKLE ones — the wildcard above is .json only,
# so a .pkl tape cache (nav-cook's is 58MB) sailed past it into `git add`.
scripts/.*.pkl

# test artifacts
.coverage
# [2026-07-30 (gp)] coverage.json is a BUILD ARTIFACT. CI generates it
# (tests.yml: `coverage json -o coverage.json`) and passes it to
# audit_coverage_floors.py explicitly. A committed one is junk at best:
# I committed a 1-module, 10.6% run by accident via `git add -A`, and a
# local audit run would then grade the real-money floors against it.
coverage.json
.pytest_cache/
htmlcov/
__pycache__/

# machine-local Claude permission list — it stores commands VERBATIM, so any
# command containing a secret becomes a stored secret. Untracked 2026-07-22
# after a live DB password accumulated into it (see CHANGELOG cc).
.claude/settings.local.json
scripts/.books_cohort_cache/
scripts/.band_kelly_cache/
scripts/.divstudy_cache/
scripts/.sqz_cache/
scripts/.ladder_cache/
scripts/.band_kelly_horizon_cache/
scripts/.ext_veto_cache/

# [(aan)] study tape caches — a registered selftest module writes megabytes
# of venue candles beside itself; untracked and unignored is one `git add -A`
# away from being committed.
scripts/.*_tape*/
